{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-74645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{2}{5-3\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-74645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $5-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $5+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $5+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{2}{5-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{5+3\\text{i}}{5+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+6\\text{i}}{25+15\\text{i}-15\\text{i}-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+6\\text{i}}{25-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+6\\text{i}}{25-(9)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+6\\text{i}}{25+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+6\\text{i}}{34}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10+6\\text{i}}{34}=\\frac{10}{34}+\\frac{6}{34}\\text{i}=\\frac{5}{17}+\\frac{3}{17}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-74645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "959115c334b3f125a13d3c6db5f6c33bfb228fe6ab4208f6d9430be54f0bbf7e"} {"question" "q-74645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-74645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3}{17}-\\frac{5}{17}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{17}+\\frac{3}{17}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{17}+\\frac{5}{17}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{17}+\\frac{3}{17}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{17}-\\frac{3}{17}\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-74645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{17}+\\frac{3}{17}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-74653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${z}_{1}=5-2\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=3\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-74653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5-2\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $3\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+3\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-3\\text{i},$ or simply $-3\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{5-2\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-2\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3\\text{i}}{-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15\\text{i}+6{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15\\text{i}+6(-1)}{-9(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6-15\\text{i}}{9}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6-15\\text{i}}{9}=-\\frac{6}{9}-\\frac{15}{9}\\text{i}=-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{5}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-74653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "959115c334b3f125a13d3c6db5f6c33bfb228fe6ab4208f6d9430be54f0bbf7e"} {"question" "q-74653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-74653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{5}{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{5}{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{5}{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-74653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{5}{3}\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $1+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-3\\text{i}}{1-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}-15{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}-15(-1)}{1-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}+15}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{15+5\\text{i}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{15+5\\text{i}}{10}=(\\frac{3}{2})+(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "959115c334b3f125a13d3c6db5f6c33bfb228fe6ab4208f6d9430be54f0bbf7e"} {"question" "q-316847" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316847" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316847" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316847" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{8}{3+4\\text{i}}=($\n {{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $3+4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3-4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3+4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{8}{3+4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3-4\\text{i}}{3-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8(3-4\\text{i})}{{3}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24-32\\text{i}}{9-(-16)} \\\\  & =\\frac{24-32\\text{i}}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{24-32\\text{i}}{25}=(\\frac{24}{25})+(-\\frac{32}{25})\\,\\text{i}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "959115c334b3f125a13d3c6db5f6c33bfb228fe6ab4208f6d9430be54f0bbf7e"} {"question" "q-316866" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316866" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{24}{25}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316866" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316866" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{32}{25}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{4}{-2-3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-2-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{-2-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{4}{-2-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2+3\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(-2+3\\text{i})}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8+12\\text{i}}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8+12\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-8+12\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{8}{13})+(\\frac{12}{13})\\,\\text{i}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "959115c334b3f125a13d3c6db5f6c33bfb228fe6ab4208f6d9430be54f0bbf7e"} {"question" "q-316875" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316875" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{8}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316875" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"} {"question" "q-316875" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b46510ab5c32e50171e70d2d4fb07b4150c942278c66095e81683506612f068"}] "usage" {} "basis" 666 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
